  "description": "Valid normalize reports (report format v1, docs/M2_DATA_CONTRACT.md section 5.10), constructed for illustration with the capture identifier of the constructed raw-record examples; no value is taken from a capture, and the hashes are placeholders. report_segments shows a run over two raw files (120000 and 60000 records before their file_end records) on three sockets: the first carries segment 0 (records 0:12 to 1:41000, cut by a checksum mismatch at 1:41001, after which the runner's note, unsubscribe and subscribe are records 1:41002 to 1:41004 and the old subscription's book messages 1:41005 to 1:41007 are dropped while unsynced) and segment 1 (too short, cut when that socket closed at 1:41201); the second socket, opened at 1:41202, is refused under R9 (a socket rejection that uses up no segment index); the third carries segment 2, refused under R2 and ended by the planned end (its ws_close capture_end is record 1:59999, which is no cut). It lists every dropped and count key, in the order the schema lists them; its canonical bytes sort every object's keys (section 5.10), and the tests serialize it with canonicalReport. report_no_fixture shows a run refused at the capture level (R1b) that was given --supersedes; report_r1_unsupported_version shows a run whose raw manifest declares an unsupported capture format version. Both carry no segments, cuts, dropped items or counts. tests/schemas.test.ts validates each example against schemas/normalize-report.v1.schema.json and derives the deliberate failure cases from them.",
